<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Organic_Chemistry/Organic_Chemistry_(Morsch_et_al.)/27:_Biomolecules_-_Lipids/27.02:_Soap" class="mt-section"><span id="Exercise_.5C(.5CPageIndex.7B2.7D.5C)"></span><h5 class="box-legend" id="Exercise_.5C(.5CPageIndex.7B2.7D.5C)-36483"><span class="lt-icon-default">Exercise \(\PageIndex{2}\)</span></h5>

<p>Draw the structure of calcium stearate, a component of soap scum.</p>

<dl>
    <dt><strong class="emphasis bold">Answer</strong></dt>
    <dd>
    <p>(C<sub>17</sub>H<sub>35</sub>COO)<sub>2</sub>Ca<sup>2</sup><sup>+</sup></p>
    </dd>
</dl>
</div></section>
